---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../styles/doge.css';
import '../../styles/lgr.css';
---

<Layout
  title="Lancashire: open-data tools for the county | Tom Pickup"
  description="A growing set of open-data tools for Lancashire, starting with the Business Observatory: the county's business economy in public data, area by area and under the four new unitary councils arriving in 2028."
>
  <div class="doge-page">
    <nav class="doge-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span class="sep">/</span>
      <span class="here">Lancashire</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="doge-head">
      <span class="doge-eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> Lancashire</span>
      <h1 class="doge-title">Open-data tools for Lancashire</h1>
      <p class="doge-sub">
        A growing set of tools that read the county through the public data it already leaves behind. Each one is
        built the same way: every figure carries its source and its date. This section starts with the Business
        Observatory, and more Lancashire tools will join it here over time.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="doge-section">
      <h2 class="doge-h2">Explore</h2>
      <div class="doge-grid">
        <a class="doge-card" href="/lancashire/business/">
          <div class="doge-card-kicker">Business Observatory</div>
          <div class="doge-card-title">The Lancashire economy</div>
          <div class="doge-card-desc">The county's business base in public data: company distress, high-growth firms, where the council pound lands, and innovation money, area by area and under the 2028 unitary boundaries.</div>
          <span class="doge-card-go">Open the Observatory &rarr;</span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="doge-note" style="margin-top:1.1rem;">
        More Lancashire tools are on the way and will appear here as they are built.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
